WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:03.320
- Whatever you do, don't
be rude to the people

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.550
handling your food because you might find

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:07.033
a pubic hair in your burger.

00:00:07.109 --> 00:00:09.692
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.020
- How do you get something for free?

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:16.930
B.Y.O.B. bring your own bug. (chuckles)

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.413
- Complain, first off, but you don't even

00:00:18.413 --> 00:00:19.710
have to complain that much,

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:20.820
you don't even have to make a scene.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.400
Open the package and
take one bite of the food

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.700
and then return it and
they can't take it back

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:27.110
over the counter most of the time,

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:28.793
so you're just gonna
get free food that way.

00:00:28.793 --> 00:00:30.630
- Some of the managers
at some of the spots,

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.280
sometimes they have coupons that they have

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:33.640
in their back pocket and they give out

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.690
whenever they feel like
they're in good spirits.

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:38.640
So if you see a manager when
you walk into a spot, be nice.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.373
- [Woman] What time is best to order food?

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:44.070
- The best time to order
food is right when they open.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.980
- Breakfast, you wanna order
it as early as possible.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.840
If you get breakfast towards
the end of the breakfast time,

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:53.713
you're getting the worst, oldest, stalest,

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.420
grossest eggs ever,
you're getting them nasty.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.750
If you're gonna be buying
food for lunch or dinner,

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:00.760
you wanna do that outside of the rush hour

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.120
because the rush hour is
when we don't pay attention

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.470
to the quality of the food.

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:06.913
Do ice cream machines really break?

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:08.420
All the time.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:10.963
They are the worst machines ever made.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.980
They get jammed, nobody likes them.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.580
We hate that you buy ice cream.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:18.040
- Sometimes like we don't have people

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.300
who either don't know
how to use the machine.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.040
Sometimes people are just
lazy and don't feel like

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.850
walking over to the
machine and they'll lie

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.393
and say it's broke.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.950
- [Woman] Are you told to
fill cups with ice on purpose

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:31.280
or not fill up cartons
with fries to the top?

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:32.980
- We're gonna fill up a
lot of ice in that cup

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.190
because you're gonna get less soda.

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:35.410
If you're gonna go to a place,

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:37.930
go to one where you can get
your own soda out of the machine

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.420
because that's the only way
to cheat the system on that.

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:43.060
- For fries, if we
haven't made a new batch

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:45.453
and it's like the scraps
of the last batch,

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.520
we'll just try to get
what's last in there.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:51.340
- We always, always, always
didn't fill them to the top.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:52.400
We did that on purpose.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.140
If we ever did it, we got in trouble.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:55.563
Our boss did not like that.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:56.780
- What are the consequences

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:59.703
if you put soda in a free water cup?

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:01.840
Diabetes? (chuckles)

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.389
- You get arrested immediately.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.380
(siren wails)
No, I'm kidding.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.090
They don't do anything at all.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:08.020
Don't do the brown sodas because

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.000
then it doesn't look as conspicuous.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.760
- If there's a manager standing by you,

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.270
maybe they might call
you out and you might get

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:16.593
a little shamed, a water cup shaming.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:20.010
- Are the employees must wash hand sign

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:21.740
more of a reminder for you

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.073
or to make customers feel better?

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.380
It's for all of us.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.410
We shouldn't have to remind you as adults

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:30.453
to wash your hands, but we all
should just wash our hands.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:32.260
- They think that sign's
just gonna throw it out there

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:34.020
and make the customers
immediately think oh,

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.750
of course they're washing their
hands, they're so hygienic.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:38.280
Yeah, that's not always the case.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.070
- There are some people that
might not wash their hands

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:42.030
because they wear gloves and might just

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:44.040
put on gloves on top of their dirty hands

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.860
like oh, what do I need
to wash my hands for?

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:48.783
You idiot, you just put on
gloves with your dirty hands.

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:50.930
- So if you ever see
anybody handle your food,

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:54.800
make sure that they're wearing
gloves every single time.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.030
I'm not gonna tell you why,

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:58.630
I'm just gonna say make
sure they're wearing gloves.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:00.350
- Are names misleading?

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:04.200
Does fresh always mean fresh? (laughs)

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.833
I plead the fifth on that question.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:08.500
- Names being misleading, yeah.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.340
There's a lot of fake lines
that are put on those burgers

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:12.910
to think that they're
going through a flame,

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:15.660
they're not, there's no fire
that touches those things.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:20.370
- Have you ever created your
own secret menu, what was it?

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:22.350
If you're lactose intolerant like me

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:24.290
and you don't want cheese
on your baked potato,

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.110
barbecue sauce is the way to go.

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:28.970
It's like a big, giant
barbecue potato chip.

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:32.170
- I would always get the
ice cream concoctions.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.180
I would throw salty stuff in it like fries

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.930
because I'm fat and customers
saw that I made that

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:38.683
and they wanted it but we
couldn't make it for them

00:03:38.683 --> 00:03:40.940
because it wasn't actually on the menu.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:43.660
- You just get creative, you
mix some spicy with some sweet,

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.110
some hot with some cold, just
see what you can come up with.

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:49.203
The combinations are endless.

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:52.473
- What's the most annoying
thing you get asked daily?

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:55.408
How many patties are on
a double cheeseburger?

00:03:55.408 --> 00:03:56.241
(crickets chirp)

00:03:56.241 --> 00:03:57.960
- Ordering on the phone
is annoying because

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.520
either you're trying to talk to me

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:00.720
or you're trying to talk
to the other person.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.710
- You know they're from
Canada when they want mayo

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:04.953
for their fries, that's disgusting.

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:07.227
- Be nice to the people
that are making your food.

00:04:07.227 --> 00:04:10.003
Got it, one more time for
the people in the back,

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:12.400
be nice to the people
that are making your food

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:14.130
because they're making your food, dude,

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:16.080
like seriously, and
you're not sitting there

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.480
watching what they're doing.

